\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Workman Of God! O lose not heart,
\par But learn what God is like,
\par And in the darkest battle- field
\par Thou shalt know where to strike
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thrice blest is he to whom is given
\par The instinct that can tell
\par That God is on the field when He
\par Is most invisible.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. For God is other than we think;
\par His ways are far above,
\par Far beyond reason's height, andreached
\par Only by childlike love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Then learn to scorn the praise of man,
\par And learn to lose with God;
\par For Jesus won the world through shame,
\par And beckons thee His road.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For right is right, since God is God,
\par And right the day must win;
\par To doubt would be disloyalty,
\par To falter would be sin.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

